 ## Overview
-This method assigns the type of each voxel in a procedural world based on its vertical position relative to the generated terrain surface (`genHeight`) and biome parameters derived from noise functions (moisture, temperature, wackiness) [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of creating varied, biologically plausible terrain structures (such as underwater layers, deserts, and jungles) without hard-coding specific coordinates. It differs from its sibling [Procedural Tree Generation](4826-procedural-tree-generation.md) by focusing on static ground composition and layering rather than organic structure placement, and builds on [Chunk Generation with Base Terrain](52-chunk-generation-with-base-terrain.md) which provides the underlying heightmap [S1, unofficial].
